Okay then, if I could make the arrangements and choose one figure from each of five different centuries, I’d go with:

1. Marco Polo (13th century) because he’s always been an inspiration to me with his travels and stories, which I consider fascinating;
2. Leonardo da Vinci (15th century) because he’s such an interesting historical figure and a true Renaissance man, and I can imagine many interesting conversations with him about his works of art;
3. Queen Elizabeth I of England (16th century), as she is one of the most important historical queens and I would very much like her company while sipping on some excellent wine during the course of this meal;
4. Napoleon Bonaparte (18th century) who is famous in history books and known as a military general, and perhaps also as a lover of good food (though I’ve never checked that on Wikipedia);
5. Marilyn Monroe (20th century) who has inspired artists and poets with her beauty, acting, and singing talents, and would likely bring a lot of joy to the table.

I think they might be able to have fun telling each other stories of their lives, their experiences and adventures, their thoughts on history and what lies ahead. It’s just going to be a really amazing experience.
